# SwiftLint / CI parity (mandatory for agents)

CI runs **soft** SwiftLint (`.swiftlint.yml`, zero violations) via `bundle exec fastlane lint` before/alongside tests. Agents must run the same gate when changing Swift sources — not only `fastlane test`.

## Required (repo root)

```bash
brew install swiftlint   # once per machine if missing
bundle exec fastlane lint
bundle exec fastlane test
```

Equivalent without Fastlane (same soft config):

```bash
bash scripts/ci/swiftlint.sh
```

## Soft vs strict

| Config | File | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| Soft (CI) | `.swiftlint.yml` | Must stay **0** violations |
| Strict | `.swiftlint-strict.yml` | Inventory / progressive cleanup only |

Do **not** fail the soft gate by re-enabling rules without fixing violations. Work the epic: `docs/tasks/pending/task-epic-swiftlint-cleanup.md` (+ inventory md/json).

Refresh strict inventory when closing a rule-group subtask:

```bash
swiftlint lint --config .swiftlint-strict.yml --reporter summary
```

## Do NOT

- Skip lint because “tests passed”
- Point CI or agents at `.swiftlint-strict.yml` until soft ≈ agreed strict set
- Lower soft standards by blanketing `disable` comments without an epic note

